</style></div><div class="layout_2-col_layout u-grid-breakout"><div class="layout_2-col_content"><div class="layout_2-col_title_wrap"><div data-fade-in="true" data-split-heading="false" data-number="40" data-wf--typography-heading--font-style="h5" class="u-text w-variant-326a9562-3263-06da-e8ef-16981fd70f1c w-richtext u-margin-bottom-6 u-color-accent"><li><strong>Introducing the Augscheller Family</strong></li></div><div data-number="14" data-split-heading="true" class="layout_2-col_title u-text-style-h1">Magdalena</div></div><div data-fade-in="true" class="layout_2-col_text_wrap"><div data-fade-in="false" data-number="44" data-wf--typography-paragraph--font-style="inherit" class="u-text w-richtext u-rich-text"><p>After graduating from the Kaiserhof Hotel Management School in Merano, Magdalena joined the family business directly. Since then, she has welcomed our guests with great warmth, guided them through their stay, and ensured <strong>a personal and attentive service in the evenings.</strong></p><p>In summer, Magdalena is often out in the mountains and happily shares her favorite <strong>hiking tips </strong>with our guests. In the evenings, she complements every menu with a suitable <strong>wine recommendation.</strong></p><p>In winter, she works as a ski instructor on the slopes, combining her love of movement with her <strong>deep connection to the region.</strong></p><p><strong>My motto:<br/></strong>&quot;Nature is my balance.&quot;</p><p><strong>What I enjoy doing:</strong><br/>I love spending my free time outdoors in nature or exploring the world and discovering new cultures.</p><p><strong>My favorite spot in the Passeier Valley:</strong><br/>The Jaufen Peak</p><p><strong>You can usually find me at the Jägerhof:</strong><br/>At the reception or during the evening service</p></div></div></div><div class="layout_2-col_visual"><div data-theme-image-wrap="" data-position="right" data-number="30" class="layout_2-col_visual_foreground u-ratio-4-5"><div data-wf-